<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Artanes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 95 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Artanes was the last king of Sophene, a small Armenian kingdom on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a>, descended according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> from the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zariadres">Zariadres</a>. Around 95 BCE he was deposed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigranes-the-great">Tigranes the Great</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, who annexed Sophene and united most Armenian lands under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artaxiad-dynasty">Artaxiad dynasty</a> at the start of his rapid expansion.</p></div>
